01:18:46.291 --> 01:18:47.665
some that sort of
caused people problems,

01:18:47.666 --> 01:18:48.990
but if a car is trying to

01:18:48.991 --> 01:18:51.435
decide which person to
kill its classification-

01:18:51.436 --> 01:18:53.630
&gt;&gt; So here's what I think
we should do about cars.

01:18:53.631 --> 01:18:55.610
Is that your question or not?

01:18:55.611 --> 01:19:04.305
&gt;&gt; Well, I mean, what
are you going to say?

01:19:04.306 --> 01:19:07.425
&gt;&gt; Oh, thank you. All right.

01:19:07.426 --> 01:19:09.460
So for a while, I
thought "Oh my God,

01:19:09.461 --> 01:19:11.130
we can't do anything
until we figure

01:19:11.131 --> 01:19:13.260
out what's right to do
in all situations."

01:19:13.261 --> 01:19:15.480
Then thinking about the cars,

01:19:15.481 --> 01:19:18.795
I thought well suppose
you have an algorithm

01:19:18.796 --> 01:19:25.385
that what you do is you learn
what do average people do.

01:19:25.386 --> 01:19:27.730
Maybe you used
the Moral Machine for this.

01:19:27.731 --> 01:19:28.840
Maybe you have some other way of

01:19:28.841 --> 01:19:30.910
figuring out statistically which

01:19:30.911 --> 01:19:34.170
you learn what sort of
a random person would do.

01:19:34.171 --> 01:19:36.030
And then your car
driving algorithm

01:19:36.031 --> 01:19:37.245
should do the following,

01:19:37.246 --> 01:19:39.980
when it gets into one of
these really touchy situations,

01:19:39.981 --> 01:19:41.650
it should do what
a random person does,

01:19:41.651 --> 01:19:42.800
and the rest of
the time, it should

01:19:42.801 --> 01:19:44.480
just do it automated driving.

01:19:44.481 --> 01:19:47.500
So this would be much better than

01:19:47.501 --> 01:19:50.430
